## Blackjack rules

- **Goal:** beat dealer without exceeding 21. 2–10 face; J/Q/K = 10; Ace = 1 or 11. **Soft hand** = Ace counted as 11 without busting.
- **Flow:** bet → deal two each → player (hit / stand / double / split) → dealer reveals hole, draws to 17 → compare. Natural blackjack pays **3:2**. **Push** = tie.
- Dealer 17: one constant — stand on all 17s **or** hit soft 17 (`HIT_SOFT_17`).

## Basic strategy (**rules of thumb** — tables vary by decks / S17 / DAS)

- **Hard:** 8− hit; 9 double vs 3–6 else hit; 10 double vs 2–9; 11 double vs 2–10; 12 hit vs 2–3, stand vs 4–6; 13–16 stand vs 2–6 else hit; 17+ stand.
- **Soft:** A2–A3 double vs 5–6 else hit; A4–A5 double vs 4–6 else hit; A6 double vs 3–6 else hit; A7 stand vs 2,7,8 / double vs 3–6 / hit vs 9–A; A8–A9 stand.
- **Pairs:** always split A,A and 8,8; never split 10s or 5s; split 2,3,6,7 vs low dealer; split 9s except vs 7,10,A; 4s rarely.
- **Double:** prefer 10/11 and soft doubles vs weak upcards when allowed.

Label advice as **rules of thumb** in comments/UI.

